<title>JAPAN: BOJ sees Sept money market surplus 1.57 trln yen.</title>
<headline>BOJ sees Sept money market surplus 1.57 trln yen.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's money market is expected to have a 1.57 trillion yen surplus in September, up from a deficit of 531.8 billion yen a year earlier, the Bank of Japan (BOJ) said in a statement on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Details, excluding expected government bond issues, were as follows in billions of yen (figures may not tally due to rounding and minor factors):  </p>
<p>						  Sept 96     Sept 95</p>
<p> Bank Notes					-200	 +33.6</p>
<p> Fiscal Funds				  +1,770	-565.4</p>
<p>    Grants to local governments	  +4,010    +3,819.0</p>
<p>    Redemption of government bonds     +2,670    +2,696.6</p>
<p>    Social security			    +500	+464.2</p>
<p>    Public finance corporation	     +220    -1,942.4</p>
<p>    Insurance				  -2,580    -2,557.1</p>
<p>    Taxes					-3,910    -3,708.4</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    Total					+1,570	-531.8</p>
</text>
